The PIR OUT pin, read once per pass, is LOW, HIGH, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, LOW in turn. What does the serial monitor show when this code runs?

```
bool onceki = false;

void setup() {
  pinMode(2, INPUT);
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  bool h = (digitalRead(2) == HIGH);
  if (h && !onceki) Serial.println("A");
  if (!h && onceki) Serial.println("B");
  onceki = h;
}
```

We want the LED to light when there is motion. The PIR module is wired correctly, but when the Motion box is ticked the LED is off, and when it is unticked the LED is on. Which line is wrong?

```
const int PIR = 2;

void setup() {
  pinMode(PIR, INPUT);
  pinMode(13, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  digitalWrite(13, digitalRead(PIR) == LOW);
}
```
